 "annotations": [
  {
   "id": "row-0",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -150,
   "w": 620,
   "text": "FIRST TEN MINUTES\nThree questions — city, interests, then four either/or picks — and we import what they already saved. The app is full before they ever see Home."
  },
  {
   "id": "row-1000",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 850,
   "w": 620,
   "text": "THE APP — PHOTO WHEN WE HAVE ONE\nCategory icon + serif title + one meta line + a reason. When extraction returned a usable photo the icon tile becomes the photo; when it didn't, nothing breaks and the row reads exactly as before (ADR 0024). Home has a real zero-data state — the app is never empty."
  },
  {
   "id": "row-2000",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 1850,
   "w": 620,
   "text": "CAPTURE — SAVE FIRST, UNDERSTAND AFTER\nThe save is safe before any AI runs. The reason chip is memory input, not a setting. When the match is weak we ask instead of guessing, and it stays saved either way."
  },
  {
   "id": "row-3000",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 2850,
   "w": 620,
   "text": "BRINGING IT BACK\nThe half that makes saving worth anything. Reminders are tied to the reason it was saved, not to a generic timer. A trip is a shape for saves that already exist."
  },
  {
   "id": "row-4000",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 3850,
   "w": 620,
   "text": "VOICE, ASKING, AND WHAT WE LEARNED\nVoice is a way into memory, not just search. Ask answers only from your own saves. Your taste says which parts you told us and which parts we worked out."
  },
  {
   "id": "row-5000",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 4850,
   "w": 620,
   "text": "WHEN IT DOES NOT WORK\nEvery failure says what happened and offers the way out. None is a dead end, and none loses the save (mobile PRD §50)."
  }
 ],
